# Push Workflow

Always work on `main`. There is no staging branch.

A bare **push** means: commit on `main`, push to GitHub, **and** deploy to Vercel. This overrides any general rule that treats "push" as commit and `git push` only. The same applies to "ship", "deploy" and "push all branches":

1. **Commit** all relevant changes on `main` with a clear message.
2. **Push and deploy** with `npm run ship`. Don't use a bare `git push`. It pushes `main`, verifies `origin/main` is that exact commit, replaces duplicate Git builds for that commit with a cached direct Vercel deployment, and verifies `www.studiobetonika.com` is live on it. See the Releases section of `AGENTS.md`.

Report success only after `npm run ship` confirms the live deployment. Give its build time and end-to-end time separately.

## Variants

| User says | Action |
|-----|-----|
| "push" / "ship" / "deploy" | commit main → `npm run ship` (push to GitHub and deploy to Vercel) |
| "just commit" / "commit only" | commit only |
| "do not deploy" | commit only; any push to `main` triggers a Vercel Git deployment |
| "push without deploying" | explain that pushing `main` deploys via Git, and ask before pushing |

For any other phrasing, follow the user's exact wording.
